$post_body = <<<'HTML'
<p>Honeycomb shades are better than roller shades for energy efficiency because their cellular structure traps insulating air against the glass, while a roller shade is a single flat layer of fabric with no air pocket at all. Roller shades still have real advantages in cost and a clean, minimal look, so the better choice depends on whether energy performance or price and style come first. Homeowners asking whether roller shades or honeycomb shades fit a specific room are really asking which tradeoff matters more for that window. Both lines are part of the window treatments carried by <a href="%BASE%/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Creative Blinds and Drapes</a>, and the <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/roller-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">roller shades</a> collection in particular is a popular starting point for budget-conscious homeowners.</p>
%IMAGE1%
<h2 id="where-roller-shades-still-make-sense">Where Roller Shades Still Make Sense</h2>
<p><strong>Roller shades are not an energy product, but they solve other problems well.</strong></p>
<ul class="bp-list">
  <li>A lower price point than most honeycomb shades of the same size.</li>
  <li>A flatter, more minimal look that suits modern or open-concept rooms.</li>
  <li>Easy cleaning, since a flat fabric surface has no folds to collect dust.</li>
  <li>Fast turnaround on simple light-filtering or blackout fabric choices.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="where-honeycomb-shades-pull-ahead-on-performance">Where Honeycomb Shades Pull Ahead on Performance</h2>
<p>The <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/honeycomb-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">honeycomb shades</a> line exists specifically to address the energy gap that flat shades leave behind:</p>
<ul class="bp-list">
  <li>Trapped air cells raise the window's effective R-value more than any flat fabric can.</li>
  <li>Double cell versions add a second air layer for an even bigger gain.</li>
  <li>Energy performance holds up in both winter heat loss and summer heat gain.</li>
  <li>The added insulation can reduce the draft felt near a window on cold days.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="how-does-installation-differ-between-the-two">How Does Installation Differ Between the Two?</h2>
<p>Both roller shades and honeycomb shades mount the same way on most windows, so the install process itself is not a major factor in the decision.</p>
<ul class="bp-list">
  <li>Inside-mount brackets work for both styles on a standard window frame.</li>
  <li>Honeycomb shades sit slightly deeper in the frame due to the folded fabric.</li>
  <li>Roller shades have a lower profile headrail, which suits a minimal trim look.</li>
  <li>Both styles are available in cordless and motorized versions with similar installation time.</li>
</ul>
%IMAGE2%
<h2 id="roller-shades-vs-honeycomb-shades-at-a-glance">Roller Shades vs Honeycomb Shades at a Glance</h2>
<div class="compare-table-wrap">
<table class="compare-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Roller Shades</th><th>Honeycomb Shades</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Energy performance</td><td>Minimal</td><td>Strong</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Typical price</td><td>Lower</td><td>Moderate to higher</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Look</td><td>Flat, minimal</td><td>Soft, folded texture</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Best use case</td><td>Budget rooms, simple style</td><td>Rooms with high heat gain or loss</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sound dampening</td><td>Little</td><td>Noticeable, especially double cell</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>For a window where the monthly utility bill matters most, honeycomb shades are the stronger pick, while roller shades remain a solid, lower-cost option for rooms where style and simplicity matter more than insulation. A member of the team can help weigh the two for a specific room, and anyone ready to move forward can <a href="%BASE%/contact/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">schedule a free in-home consultation</a> to compare samples in natural light. Our guide on <a href="%BASE%/blog/are-blinds-or-shades-better/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">whether blinds or shades perform better overall</a> looks at the wider product categories beyond just these two shade styles.</p>
HTML;

